<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Temporal Backtracking Search (TBS)</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Leveraging the conditional reuse gap, TBS performs state-space search directly over temporal prefixes. The search maintains a <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">priority frontier</span> <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, a pool of verified prefix anchors awaiting expansion. Each entry in <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> is a tuple <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(K,\mathbf{v}_{1:R},\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(K,\mathbf{v}_{1:R},\pi)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{1:R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{1:R}</annotation></semantics></math> is the verified prefix, <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=R/\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=R/\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is its corresponding latent length (Section <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Variable-𝐾 Conditioning ‣ 3 Method ‣ Temporal Backtracking Search for Test-time Generative Video Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>), and <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is a deterministic priority score assigned by the verifier (higher <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> indicates a more promising anchor for continuation). Instead of repeatedly querying the computationally expensive <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathrm{root}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>root</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{root}}</annotation></semantics></math>, TBS isolates localized failures and samples continuations strictly from anchors stored in <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Guided by a process-level verifier <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> (Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3.1 Problem Formulation and the Conditional Reuse Gap ‣ 3 Method ‣ Temporal Backtracking Search for Test-time Generative Video Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), the search proceeds as follows. For each rollout, <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> evaluates the exact-match status and extracts the first failure frame <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>, an aligned restart anchor <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\leq F{-}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\leq F{-}1</annotation></semantics></math>, and the priority score <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. If an invalid rollout contains reusable progress (<math id="S3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>), the corresponding tuple is inserted into <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. At each expansion step, TBS pops the highest-priority anchor from <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> and queries the generator for <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> candidate suffix continuations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For latent diffusion models, the restart frame must strictly align with the VAE’s temporal latent factor <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. The aligned restart anchor is computed as <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\mathbf{v})=\tau\cdot\lfloor(F(\mathbf{v})-1)/\tau\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\mathbf{v})=\tau\cdot\lfloor(F(\mathbf{v})-1)/\tau\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>. This guarantees the generator cleanly resumes from exactly <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=R/\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=R/\tau</annotation></semantics></math> latent frames, preventing temporal overlap or information leakage between the clean prefix and the resampled suffix.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Variable-<math id="S3.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> Conditioning</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For TBS to function, the generator must support temporal branching: given a prefix verified up to frame <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, the model must synthesize the suffix while preserving the exact prefix conditioning. Standard video diffusion models lack this capability, as they denoise all frames jointly from a single-frame initial condition (<math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{=}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{=}1</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To unlock temporal branching while keeping per-branch inference cost constant, we finetune the video diffusion model (based on Wan2.2-TI2V-5B<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>) with
<span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">variable-<math id="S3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> conditioning</span>. Let <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}=\mathcal{E}(\mathbf{v})\in\mathbb{R}^{C\times T_{z}\times H_{z}\times W_{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}=\mathcal{E}(\mathbf{v})\in\mathbb{R}^{C\times T_{z}\times H_{z}\times W_{z}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the VAE-encoded latent representation. During training, we apply a per-frame timestep mask: the first <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>
latent frames remain clean (<math id="S3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>), while the remaining suffix frames are noised at a single sampled timestep <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{i}=\begin{cases}\mathbf{z}_{i}&amp;i\leq K,\\
(1-t)\,\mathbf{z}_{i}+t\,\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{i},\quad\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})&amp;i&gt;K,\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{i}=\begin{cases}\mathbf{z}_{i}&amp;i\leq K,\\
(1-t)\,\mathbf{z}_{i}+t\,\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{i},\quad\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})&amp;i&gt;K,\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">At inference, <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is dictated by the verifier’s restart anchor (<math id="S3.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=R/\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=R/\tau</annotation></semantics></math>). We finetune the base video diffusion model with a progressive curriculum that shifts the training distribution
from <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{=}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{=}1</annotation></semantics></math> to a broad mixture up to <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{=}20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{=}20</annotation></semantics></math>. Without this curriculum, the model collapses when conditioned on longer
prefixes (Appendix <a href="#A2.SS2" title="B.2 Training and Inference Details ‣ Appendix B Structured Video Reasoning Details ‣ Temporal Backtracking Search for Test-time Generative Video Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">A naive branching alternative is extracting the last verified frame to use as a <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{=}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{=}1</annotation></semantics></math> initial condition. However, a single static frame strips away the motion, dynamics, and task momentum established by the preceding trajectory. To isolate the necessity of motion context, we evaluated a controlled subset of 40 provably repairable long-horizon Maze trajectories. Replacing the full temporal prefix with a single-frame state reset collapsed the repair success rate from <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100\%</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.5\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.5</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.5\%</annotation></semantics></math> (Appendix <a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1 Prefix-Conditioning Ablation ‣ Appendix B Structured Video Reasoning Details ‣ Temporal Backtracking Search for Test-time Generative Video Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>). Full prefix conditioning is therefore the foundational engine enabling temporal backtracking.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experiments</h2>

<figure id="S4.F3" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_center">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F3.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 3</span>: </span><span id="S4.F3.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Evaluation domains.<span id="S4.F3.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Rule-based grid-worlds: </span>2D Maze<span id="S4.F3.12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (a), </span>3D Maze<span id="S4.F3.12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (b), </span>Keys-and-Doors<span id="S4.F3.12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (c), </span>Sliding Puzzle<span id="S4.F3.12.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (d), </span>Sokoban<span id="S4.F3.12.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (e); continuous navigation </span>Target-Bench<span id="S4.F3.12.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (f); robotic manipulation </span>RoboTwin<span id="S4.F3.12.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (g).</span></span></figcaption><img src="2606.13861v1/domain.png" id="S4.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/203;" width="476" height="203" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Experimental Setup</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate TBS in three regimes spanning the spectrum of process supervision available in practice: exact symbolic verification in rule-based grid-worlds, learned trajectory prediction in continuous navigation, and simulator-replay verification in robotic manipulation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Structured video reasoning.</span>
We use five rule-based grid-worlds (Figure <a href="#S4.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Temporal Backtracking Search for Test-time Generative Video Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), where deterministic game rules serve as verifiers and identify the first failure frame. The domains target distinct reasoning bottlenecks: <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">2D Maze</span> and <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">3D Maze</span> for spatial path adherence, <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Sliding Puzzle</span> for semantic correctness, <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Sokoban</span> for irreversible dead states, and <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Keys-and-Doors</span> for long-horizon sub-goal ordering. Each domain has <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="600" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>600</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">600</annotation></semantics></math> evaluation samples split into easy/medium/hard; <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Keys-and-Doors</span> additionally includes a <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="300" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>300</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">300</annotation></semantics></math>-sample out-of-distribution (OOD) split with extended trajectories (Appendix <a href="#A2.SS3" title="B.3 Structured Video Reasoning Domains ‣ Appendix B Structured Video Reasoning Details ‣ Temporal Backtracking Search for Test-time Generative Video Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>, <a href="#A2.SS5" title="B.5 Verifier and Restart Details ‣ Appendix B Structured Video Reasoning Details ‣ Temporal Backtracking Search for Test-time Generative Video Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Continuous navigation.</span>
We use Target-Bench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite>, a mapless path-planning benchmark whose official score (Eq. <a href="#S4.E4" title="In 4.1 Experimental Setup ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Temporal Backtracking Search for Test-time Generative Video Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) aggregates five trajectory metrics against a ground-truth path:</p>
<table id="S4.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=0.05\,e^{-\mathrm{ADE}}+0.10\,e^{-\mathrm{FDE}}+0.10\,(1{-}\mathrm{MR}/100)+0.65\,\mathrm{SE}\cdot\mathrm{AC}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ADE</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.10</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>FDE</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.10</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>MR</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0.65</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>SE</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>AC</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=0.05\,e^{-\mathrm{ADE}}+0.10\,e^{-\mathrm{FDE}}+0.10\,(1{-}\mathrm{MR}/100)+0.65\,\mathrm{SE}\cdot\mathrm{AC},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where ADE and FDE are the average and final <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> displacement errors against the GT, MR is the percentage of trajectory points farther than <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> m from the GT, SE and AC are the benchmark’s soft-endpoint and approach-consistency scores, and TC is the trajectory-coverage term (full definitions in Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Target-Bench Navigation Details ‣ Temporal Backtracking Search for Test-time Generative Video Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>). The verifier is a learned trajectory predictor that maps the current frame and prompt to a future metric-space path, and TBS branches when the decoded video trajectory leaves the predicted spatial corridor.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Robotic manipulation.</span>
We evaluate manipulation on RoboTwin <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>, a bimanual robot benchmark backed by a physics simulator. Generated videos are decoded into 14-D action sequences via an inverse dynamics model and rolled out in the simulator, whose ground-truth task predicate serves as the verifier. RoboTwin trajectories have a natural two-phase structure—an approach phase followed by a final goal-attempt window—which TBS uses to choose restart anchors (Section <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 Mechanism: Prefix Reuse Targets Early Failure Bottlenecks ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Temporal Backtracking Search for Test-time Generative Video Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baseline and compute budget.</span>
Our baseline is Best-of-<math id="S4.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> (BoN), the standard test-time-scaling method for video generation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>, <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite>. To isolate the effect of prefix reuse, both methods share identical terminal evaluators and root candidate pools. A TBS configuration uses root width <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, child samples <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, and maximum expansions <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, giving budget <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=k_{1}+s\,(m{-}1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=k_{1}+s\,(m{-}1)</annotation></semantics></math>; we compare against BoN at matched budget <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N{=}B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N{=}B</annotation></semantics></math>. The <span id="S4.SS1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Time</span> columns in Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Temporal Backtracking Search for Test-time Generative Video Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> report normalized wall-clock cost, which grows sub-linearly due to early termination after the first verified solve.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Main Results</h3>

<figure id="S4.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 1</span>: </span><span id="S4.T1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Structured video reasoning, exact-match results.<span id="S4.T1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Reported as exact-match percentage with <math id="S4.T1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="95\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>95</mn><mo mathsize="1.110em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">95\%</annotation></semantics></math> Wilson confidence intervals; intervals are clipped at <math id="S4.T1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.T1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math>. Bold marks the better method; ties are not bolded. The TBS–BoN gap widens on <span id="S4.T1.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Hard</span> and <span id="S4.T1.7.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Strict-OOD</span> splits.</span></span></figcaption>
<table id="S4.T1.8" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T1.8.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T1.8.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.2pt 5.0pt;" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T1.8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Domain</span></th>
<th id="S4.T1.8.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.2pt 5.0pt;" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T1.8.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Split / Metric</span></th>
<td id="S4.T1.8.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.2pt 5.0pt;" colspan="2"><span id="S4.T1.8.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Baselines</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.8.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.2pt 5.0pt;" colspan="2"><span id="S4.T1.8.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Budget 10</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.8.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.2pt 5.0pt;" colspan="2"><span id="S4.T1.8.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Budget 20</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.8.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T1.8.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:-0.2pt 5.0pt;"><span id="S4.T1.8.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">BoN-1</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.8.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:-0.2pt 5.0pt;"><span id="S4.T1.8.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">BoN-5</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.8.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:-0.2pt 5.0pt;"><span id="S4.T1.8.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">BoN-10</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.8.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:-0.2pt 5.0pt;"><span id="S4.T1.8.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">TBS-10</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.8.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:-0.2pt 5.0pt;"><span id="S4.T1.8.2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">BoN-20</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.8.2.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:-0.2pt 5.0pt;"><span id="S4.T1.8.2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">TBS-20</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.8.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T1.8.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding:-0.2pt 5.0pt;" rowspan="5"><span id="S4.T1.8.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Maze</span></th>
