<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>2D Maze rich-prompt EM by shortest-path-length bin. The bins are used only for post-hoc analysis of horizon length, not as an online solution signal for TBS. The TBS gain grows monotonically with horizon: at <math id="A2.T8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="41+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>41</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">41+</annotation></semantics></math> steps, BoN-20 collapses to <math id="A2.T8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="17.1\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>17.1</mn><mo mathsize="1.110em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">17.1\%</annotation></semantics></math> while TBS-20 reaches <math id="A2.T8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="60.0\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>60.0</mn><mo mathsize="1.110em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">60.0\%</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A2.T8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+42.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>42.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+42.9</annotation></semantics></math> pp). This is the numerical table backing Figure <a href="#S4.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Temporal Backtracking Search for Test-time Generative Video Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>(a).</figcaption>
</figure>
