<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 10: </span>Failure-to-recovery distribution by trajectory-progress bin. “BoN-20 failures” rows give the distribution of failed BoN-20 root samples by their farthest verified-progress bin (sums to 100%). “TBS-20 outcomes” rows give the distribution of TBS-20 final episode outcomes; the right-most column is TBS hard-split EM. Maze and Keys-and-Doors-OOD show the strongest clustering: more than <math id="A2.T10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="70\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>70</mn><mo mathsize="1.110em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">70\%</annotation></semantics></math> of BoN failures concentrate in the earliest <math id="A2.T10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A2.T10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo mathsize="1.110em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20\%</annotation></semantics></math> bin, exactly the region where independent root sampling re-fails.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
