</section>
<section id="A2.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.9 </span>Root Solves vs. Restarted-Branch Solves</h3>

<div id="A2.SS9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section directly probes the TBS mechanism: of the episodes solved by TBS, how many were already solved by a root rollout (depth <math id="A2.SS9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>) and how many required a restarted child branch (depth <math id="A2.SS9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>). If TBS gains came purely from extra root sampling, the depth-0 share would be high; if they came from prefix reuse, the depth-<math id="A2.SS9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> share dominates.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T12" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A2.T12.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A2.T12.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T12.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T12.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Domain</span></th>
